# Subtrees clang-format must never touch. This file is the single source of
# truth for what is excluded: utility/run-clang-format.sh hands clang-format
# every tracked C/C++ source in the repository and clang-format itself skips
# the ones matched here, so the project-wide sweep, the CI check and an
# editor formatting on save all agree without a second list to keep in sync.
#
# Note the pattern repetition: clang-format matches these with POSIX fnmatch
# rules, where `*` does NOT cross a `/` and `**` is not supported (see
# clang/lib/Format/MatchFilePath.cpp). `foo/` and `foo/*` therefore do not
# match `foo/bar/baz.h` -- one glob per path depth is the only way to exclude
# a subtree. Deepest tracked path today is 4 components; 5 is headroom.

# Vendored programming-model headers (MPICH / SHMEM / NCCL / NVSHMEM), kept
# byte-identical to upstream so re-imports stay reviewable.
includesProgramModels/*
includesProgramModels/*/*
includesProgramModels/*/*/*
includesProgramModels/*/*/*/*
includesProgramModels/*/*/*/*/*

# Test inputs: their layout is often part of what is being tested, and lit RUN
# lines and line-number-sensitive diagnostics must not move.
test/*
test/*/*
test/*/*/*
test/*/*/*/*
test/*/*/*/*/*

# Enzyme-JAX's patches, copied verbatim -- see patches/README.md.
patches/*
patches/*/*

# Benchmark-suite submodules, formatted (or not) by their own repositories.
externals/*
externals/*/*
externals/*/*/*
externals/*/*/*/*
externals/*/*/*/*/*
